CVE-2023-30533
CVE-2024-22363

# Upstream vendor image CVEs. Our own images (bloom-web, langchain-agent,
# bloommcp, bloomcli, workflows, caddy, box-object-backup) have none of the
# entries below; each lists the pinned upstream images that still carry it.
# The fixes arrive with newer upstream images, not with anything built here.

# zlib1g (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# Trivy status: will_not_fix | Fixed version: none
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3 (Debian) - affects: studio
# Trivy status: affected | Fixed version: none
CVE-2025-7458

# grpc-go authz bypass - affects: gotrue, imgproxy, minio, minio-mc
# Fixed in grpc-go 1.79.3; these images have not been rebuilt with it.
CVE-2026-33186

# Go stdlib crypto/tls session resumption - affects: minio, minio-mc
# Fixed in Go 1.24.13 / 1.25.7; both binaries were built with older Go.
CVE-2025-68121

# libssl3 / libcrypto3 / openssl - affects: gotrue, postgres, storage-api
# (Alpine 3.5.5-r0) and postgres-meta, realtime, studio (Debian 12 3.0.x).
# Heap overflow on 32-bit platforms during X.509 OCTET STRING hex conversion
# of inputs over ~1.4 GiB. Every service runs on x86_64.
# Upstream: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-31789

# libgnutls30 (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# DTLS handshake out-of-bounds read (DoS only). None of these services runs a
# DTLS listener; GnuTLS is a base OS package.
# Upstream: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33845
CVE-2026-33845

# libgnutls30 (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# Authentication bypass via a NUL character in the username. None of these
# services authenticates clients through GnuTLS.
CVE-2026-42010

# python3 (OS package) - affects: storage-api, studio, supavisor
# xml.parsers.expat hash randomization entropy. The services do not run the
# OS Python on untrusted XML.
CVE-2026-7210

# libssh2-1 (Debian) - affects: realtime, studio, supavisor
# Integer overflow on large username/password arguments. No service uses SSH.
CVE-2026-7598

# perl-base (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# Heap overflow / code execution via a crafted regex. No service runs Perl on
# untrusted input; perl-base is a base OS package.
CVE-2026-13221

# perl-base (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# Archive::Tar symlink extraction. No service extracts tar archives with Perl.
CVE-2026-42496

# perl-base (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# Heap overflow when Perl compiles certain regex patterns. No service runs Perl.
CVE-2026-8376

# perl-base (Debian) - affects: postgres-meta, realtime, studio, supavisor
# Signed integer overflow in Storable (pre-3.41) during deserialization. No
# service deserializes Perl Storable data.
CVE-2026-57433

# linux-libc-dev - affects: postgrest, studio
# ksmbd signedness bug in kernel headers. Containers run the host's kernel, so
# the headers are never executed.
# Upstream: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-43185
CVE-2026-43185

# python3 (OS package) - affects: storage-api, studio, supavisor
# tarfile.extractall() filter bypass. The services do not extract untrusted
# tar archives with the OS Python.
# Upstream: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-11940
CVE-2026-11940

# tar / node-tar - affects: postgres-meta, storage-api, studio
# Gzip-bomb DoS when extracting an attacker-supplied archive. None of these
# services extracts uploaded tar archives.
CVE-2026-59873

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh — affects: caddy, gotrue, imgproxy, minio, minio-mc
# Auth bypass: an SSH server can fail to enforce a certificate's critical
# `source-address` option, letting a client connect from an address the certificate was
# meant to exclude. Reaching it needs something speaking SSH. Caddy is used here only as
# an HTTPS reverse proxy + ACME client (see caddy/Caddyfile): it serves :80, :443 and
# :2021 and runs no SSH server or client, so the affected code path is unreachable.
# The ssh code IS compiled in, rather than absent — it arrives with
# github.com/smallstep/certificates, the certificate-issuing library Caddy embeds for its
# PKI and ACME-server apps, which covers web and SSH certificates in one piece. This
# deployment enables neither app, and Caddy exposes no SSH certificate feature to enable
# in the first place. No caddy release declares a patched x/crypto yet: 2.11.3 (what we
# build) declares 0.50.0, 2.11.4 declares 0.52.0, unreleased `master` is on 0.54.0; the
# fix ships in 0.55.0. It CAN be forced at build time with
# `xcaddy build --with golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt@v0.55.0` — a subpackage path, because
# xcaddy imports whatever path it is given and golang.org/x/crypto has no code at its
# root; that spelling was verified to build and to link 0.55.0. Not taken deliberately:
# it pins the library ahead of what Caddy is tested against, for no exposure this
# deployment can reach. Reassess when a caddy release declares
# golang.org/x/crypto >= 0.55.0. See bloom#775.
# MinIO (ghcr.io/salk-harnessing-plants-initiative/minio:RELEASE.2025-01-20T14-49-07Z) links
# the same package (golang.org/x/crypto v0.32.0, with github.com/pkg/sftp) for its optional
# SFTP server, which starts only when SFTP settings are given: the `--sftp` flag, or an
# SFTP section in a `--config` file (cmd/server-main.go at that release). Both compose
# files start it as `server --console-address ":9001" /data`, with neither, so no SSH
# listener exists and the code path is unreachable. Reassess if MinIO's command gains
# `--sftp` or `--config`.
# Upstream: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-56854
CVE-2026-56854
